Subject: [PATCH] streaming_fuzzer: Allow approximate lossless Gaborish and lossy seams

Two differences between the full-frame and the streaming encode that the
per-sample threshold cannot tell from a bug:
- With Gaborish forced on, a lossless encode is only approximately lossless
  (approximate inverse Gaborish, rounded to the bit depth); both outputs can
  be most of a step away from the source, so at 1-2 bits they differ by one
  step. Allow one step at the bit depth for such samples.
- The streaming encoder sees one DC group at a time, so lossy heuristics
  (adaptive quantization, invisible pixel simplification) decide differently
  next to a DC group border. Skip samples within 8 pixels of one for lossy
  encodes.

Since libjxl#5158 (12e4bf40) lossless modular with forced Gaborish never
streams, so both encodes take the full-frame path and the first allowance is
probably dead (its reproducer passes without this patch at 12e4bf40); the
seam allowance is still needed.

diff --git a/tools/streaming_fuzzer.cc b/tools/streaming_fuzzer.cc
index cb0b977e..b6b95ad0 100644
--- a/tools/streaming_fuzzer.cc
+++ b/tools/streaming_fuzzer.cc
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <jxl/types.h>
 
 #include <array>
+#include <cmath>
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <cstdio>
 #include <cstdlib>
@@ -422,12 +423,49 @@ void Run(const FuzzSpec& spec) {
                                       0.0625f, 0.0625f, 0.0625f, 0.10f, 0.10f};
   float threshold = kThreshold[effort];
 
+  bool lossless = (spec.distance == 0.0f);
+  // Gaborish forced on makes a lossless encode only approximately lossless:
+  // the encoder applies an approximate inverse Gaborish and rounds it to the
+  // bit depth, so each output can be most of a step away from the source, and
+  // the two encoders (only the full-frame one subtracts patches first) can end
+  // up one step apart. At low bit depths, that step is larger than the
+  // threshold, so also allow one step at the bit depth.
+  Check(spec.int_options[6].flag == JXL_ENC_FRAME_SETTING_GABORISH);
+  bool lossless_gaborish = lossless && spec.int_options[6].value == 1;
+  float max_val = static_cast<float>((1u << spec.bit_depth) - 1);
+  // The streaming encoder sees one DC group at a time, so lossy heuristics
+  // (adaptive quantization, invisible pixel simplification, ...) can decide
+  // differently next to a DC group border: skip those samples.
+  Check(spec.int_options[7].flag == JXL_ENC_FRAME_SETTING_MODULAR);
+  Check(spec.int_options[17].flag ==
+        JXL_ENC_FRAME_SETTING_MODULAR_GROUP_SIZE);
+  int group_size_shift = spec.int_options[17].value;
+  size_t group_dim = (spec.int_options[7].value == 1 && group_size_shift >= 0)
+                         ? size_t{128} << group_size_shift
+                         : 256;
+  size_t dc_group_dim = group_dim * 8;
+  constexpr size_t kSeamBorder = 8;
+  const auto near_seam = [&](size_t v) {
+    return v + kSeamBorder >= dc_group_dim &&
+           (v + kSeamBorder) % dc_group_dim < 2 * kSeamBorder;
+  };
+
   int outlier_count = 0;
   for (size_t i = 0; i < dec_default.size(); ++i) {
+    size_t pixel = i / 3;
+    if (!lossless && (near_seam(pixel % spec.xsize) ||
+                      near_seam(pixel / spec.xsize))) {
+      continue;
+    }
     float d1 = Clamp1(dec_default[i], 0.0f, 1.0f);
     float d2 = Clamp1(dec_streaming[i], 0.0f, 1.0f);
     float abs_diff = std::abs(d1 - d2);
-    if (abs_diff > threshold) outlier_count++;
+    if (abs_diff <= threshold) continue;
+    if (lossless_gaborish &&
+        std::abs(std::round(d1 * max_val) - std::round(d2 * max_val)) <= 1) {
+      continue;
+    }
+    outlier_count++;
   }
   if (false) {
     fprintf(stderr, "Number of outlier values: %d / %d\n", outlier_count,
